.env
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
.superpowers/
node_modules/
apps/web/dist/

# ── AI tooling scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent settings, job scratch dirs, and the git worktrees agents run in. None of
# it describes the product, and the worktrees are whole checkouts -- committing
# them would nest the repo inside itself.
.claude/

# Plans, architecture reviews and other skill output. These are working notes
# for a session, not project documentation: docs/design/ and docs/runbooks/ are
# the documents that belong in the repo, and they stay tracked.
docs/superpowers/
architecture-review-*.html

# Agent transcripts.
*.jsonl

# ── Logo source art ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The originals the societies hand over: full-canvas exports with the mark sat
# in the middle of a lot of empty space. What the app actually serves lives in
# apps/web/public/logo/ and stays TRACKED — those are cropped, have their
# viewBox retargeted onto the ink, and are referenced by index.html and
# AppShell.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash to this one directory on purpose. A bare
# `logo/` or `*.svg` would also match apps/web/public/logo/ and quietly
# un-track the favicon and the event wordmark, which breaks the site rather
# than tidying the repo.
/apps/web/logo/
CLAUDE.md
